V9-N2 "NCR+A" (package docs/05 §1, §6: the official NCR route with the SAME trusted anchor budget).  Applies to the official NCR code
(https://github.com/XLearning-SCU/2021-NeurIPS-NCR @ 60256ba, files NCR/data.py and NCR/co_train.py).  Two changes only:
 (1) data.py: the training pairs come from the V9 OBSERVED mapping (noise.py; donors only from U, A clean) instead of the official noise index;
     the file is a numpy array of observed image indices per caption (same shape and meaning as the official t2i_index), plus an anchor mask.
     The clean labels `_labels` (used by NCR only for its printed statistics) are NOT available in the V9 setting and are set to -1 (unknown).
 (2) co_train.py: after the GMM split, every anchor pair is forced into the labeled set with clean probability 1 (the anchor-supervised term
     with weight 1), for both networks.  Nothing else changes: co-training, soft margin, the two-model averaged evaluation and the dev selection
     are the official ones.  The U pairs are treated exactly as NCR treats its noisy training set.
